  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## 12.4.0\n\n### Features\n- First release. `AppBuilder.UseMermaid()` at startup makes every `Markdown` control in the app draw closed ` ```mermaid ` fences as native diagrams. `MermaidExtension`, the Markdig extension behind it, can instead be added to one control's `Markdown.Extensions`, passed to `MarkdownSerializer`, or added to a pipeline with `MarkdownPipelineBuilder.UseMermaid()`. Flowcharts and state diagrams are drawn, with subgraphs, composite states, notes, edge labels and the `style`, `classDef` and `linkStyle` colour and stroke properties. Class diagrams (compartments, annotations, UML relationship markers, cardinalities, namespaces, notes), entity relationship diagrams (attribute rows, crow's foot cardinalities), requirement diagrams (requirement and element boxes, relationship kinds), quadrant charts (tinted quadrants, styled points), packet diagrams (bit fields in rows), kanban boards (columns, cards, priorities), user journeys (sections, scored tasks, actors), git graphs (branches, merges, cherry-picks, tags), gantt charts (time axis, task states, milestones, markers, compact mode), block diagrams (grids, groups, shapes, block arrows, links), pie charts (slices, shares, legend, showData), xy charts (bar and line series, vertical or horizontal, axis titles and range) and sequence diagrams (actors, every arrow kind, activations, notes, fragments, boxes, created and destroyed participants) are drawn too. Box series in xy charts and other diagram types show as text. Diagrams follow the light and dark theme variants with a built-in colour scheme for each (tinted rounded boxes, soft shadows, rounded edge bends, pill labels), take overrides from ordinary resources and `ThemeDictionaries` (`MarkdownMermaidNodeBackground`, `MarkdownMermaidNodeBorderBrush`, `MarkdownMermaidNodeForeground` and the like, `MarkdownMermaidShadowColor`) and redraw when one changes, use eight accent colours (`MarkdownMermaidAccent0Brush` to `MarkdownMermaidAccent7Brush`) to tell areas and series apart, draw their frontmatter or init title above them, scale down to fit a narrow view, and are parsed and laid out off the UI thread. The document is unchanged: a diagram is still a fenced code block for serialization, copy and search. Targets net8.0 and net10.0 with no package dependency beyond `Avalonia.Controls.Markdown`: the Mermaid parsers and the Sugiyama layout engine are compiled in. It depends on the `Avalonia.Controls.Markdown` package of exactly its own version, since it builds on that package's internals.",
